# ============================================================
#  Numbers (design §8.4). Tier words in effects (`mood +medium`,
#  `rel npc -small`) take their amount from `sizes`; challenge
#  difficulty tiers shift the DC from the expected skill at that
#  point of the run (`curve`, one value per turn, fitted by
#  `node tools/grim.js curve`). All values are tunable.
# ============================================================

@balance
desc: Size tiers are tiny, small, medium, large and huge; skills use the xp row.
sizes: health 3 5 10 16 25 | mood 4 8 13 20 30 | gold 3 8 15 30 60 | renown 2 4 8 13 20 | mana 3 6 10 16 25
  | alignment 3 6 10 16 25 | xp 2 3 6 10 16 | lore 1 1 3 5 8 | rel 1 2 4 6 9 | spark 4 8 13 20 30
difficulty: trivial -15 easy -7 medium 0 hard 8 heroic 16
# Skill XP (design §8.5): the next point costs a + b × level. Fitted so a balanced player averages about 55-60 at the
# end of a four-year run (L: with the spell bonus); a focused skill reaches ~65-75 by month 24 (design ~85: an alarm).
xp_cost: 1 0.04
# Rank XP needed for each promotion (Member → Officer, Officer → Captain), plus performance ≥ 70.
rank_xp: 10 25
weights: health 1 mood 1 gold 0.5 renown 0.8 mana 0.4 alignment 0 xp 1.5 rel 0.6 spark 0.4
# The combat stub (playtest 2, M39, M5): until the minigame, a fight reads arcana, vigor and guile (weighted), plus
# condition × (the mean of health, mood and mana, each as % of its max, − 50) and spells × total spell levels (at most
# +15). Entering costs mana.
combat: arcana 1 vigor 1 guile 0.5 condition 0.2 spells 0.75
combat_cost: small
# The negotiation stub (E8): until the minigame, a negotiation reads charm, lore and guile (weighted; `using` doubles one),
# plus mood and renown × their change since the run's start (as % of max). Known spells of those skills add the usual
# spell bonus (spell_check).
negotiate: charm 1 lore 1 guile 1 mood 0.15 renown 0.15
# A tonic (world expansion 1, K3): what a `boost:` state adds to the plain checks it names: one rung, about 8 points of odds
# on a normal check. Tonics share `group: tonic`, so one holds at a time; fights and negotiations never read it.
tonic: 4
# A sized boost (threads 1): `boost: kind:size` adds its size here instead of a tonic's rung, and the largest boost held
# counts. Owl's Ink, the illicit exam help, is `exam:large`: about a full grade (tools/exam-odds.js).
boost_sizes: small 4 medium 8 large 12
# How far one skill point moves a check's odds (M14): `wild` checks swing whatever your skill; `steady` ones follow it.
swing: normal 2.5 wild 1.2 steady 4
# A shift's pay (M10): `wage` in a job's cards pays the job's `pay:` at your rank × this share.
wage: short 0.5 full 1 overtime 2
# Coursework (feedback 2026-10-15): the skill XP an enrolled course gives once a term month, at course level I, II, III.
coursework: small small small
# The range a check's odds are clamped to (L-3): a 5% forced fail and a 5% forced success. Milestone checks (a
# `class: milestone` card, an exam) have no forced fail.
odds: min 5 max 95
# The check ladder (docs/authoring/checks.md, design §8.6): checks written with a rung, odds by nature and a luck word.
# A rung is the DC: who or what you're up against.
dc_tiers: novice- 0 novice 4 novice+ 8 apprentice- 12 apprentice 16 apprentice+ 20 journeyman- 24 journeyman 28
  journeyman+ 32 adept- 36 adept 40 adept+ 44 expert- 48 expert 52 expert+ 56 master- 60 master 64 master+ 68
  grandmaster- 72 grandmaster 76 grandmaster+ 80 archmage- 84 archmage 88 archmage+ 92
# Odds by nature: the chance (%) when your skill matches the DC; a circumstance step (`+1 if …`) moves it by odds_step (z).
likelihood: certain 97 sure 90 likely 70 even 50 unlikely 30 slim 15 long_shot 5 freak 1
odds_step: 0.5
# Luck: the bell's σ. Odds = floor + (ceil − floor) × Φ(z(odds) + (skill − DC) / σ); milestones run 0–100.
sigma: steady 12 normal 20 wild 32 luck 80
bell: floor 2 ceil 98
# Drift: how far the DC is pulled toward the expected skill (`curve`). Defaults: story none; milestone, crisis low; else high.
drift: none 0 low 0.15 mid 0.3 high 0.5
# A course's standard rung at levels I, II, III (a track's `standard:` overrides), and the rungs a course card rises per
# course level above its own `level:`.
course_standard: apprentice+ adept+ master+
course_step: 5
course_drift: low
# Exam preparation (L-3): a course card adds `attend` by itself (options add or cost more); each term month's
# coursework adds `monthly` (feedback 2026-10-15b: it replaced the silent per-card 2, so preparation shows); at most `cap` counts.
# 2026-10-19: `monthly` only in the three months before the exam (9 a term), and `check` instead when a check in that
# course's class is won (once a month per course); the library's revision card adds 3 a term.
study: attend 0 cap 15 monthly 3 check 5
# A course exam's difficulty at course level I, II and III: the course standard ± rungs, with low drift (checks.md).
# One rung higher since spells v2 (2026-10-17), two at II and III: the course spell, and its skill XP, now come at the
# start of each level, before its exam, not after the pass. Balanced pass rates stay about 87 / 75 / 80%.
exam_tiers: standard+2 standard+3 standard+3
# An exam's grades (feedback 2026-10-15): A from `a` over the bar, B from `b`, a pass from `pass`, each on the bell (no
# hard A gate), at `sigma` (2026-10-19: 16, was the steady 12, so skill shades the odds more gently). Going for top marks
# (`sit_exam wild`) lowers the A mark by `ambitious` and is sat at `ambitious_sigma`.
# Preparation floors (2026-10-19): the pass chance can't fall below a smooth ramp from `pass_from` to certain at
# `pass_at`, nor B-or-better below one from `b_from` to `b_at`: 12 prepared is a sure pass, 15 a sure B.
exam_bands: a 15 b 5 pass -5 ambitious 8 ambitious_sigma 20 sigma 16 pass_from 6 pass_at 12 b_from 9 b_at 15
# Peers grow with the player (feedback 2026-10-15): a character with one of these tags (classmates, and the pen pal at
# Thornwick) has every skill stat scaled up with E(turn), so that by the last month their best skill is `share` of the
# final E(turn). Faculty and villagers keep theirs.
npc_growth: share 0.9 tags peer thornwick
# A known spell adds `per` to checks of its skill (`@spell skill:`), at most `cap` (design §9.2; L-3).
spell_check: per 2 cap 6
# Learning a spell, or a level of one, gives skill XP in its skill (L-6): one tier per level of a course spell, and
# `spell_bonus_one` for a one-level spell (spells v2 §B: every other spell large).
spell_bonus: medium large huge
spell_bonus_one: large
# A forbidden spell's cast (feedback 2026-10-19): a third of its `alignment: small`, on a card and in a fight
# (combat/setup/roster.mjs ALIGNMENT_COST.forbidden keeps the same number).
forbidden_cast: alignment 2
# Spark follows friendship (M37): a friendship gain adds spark × (spark / per), at most cap× (partner× for a partner);
# spark crossing `cooldown` asks whether you want it (@game spark_cooldown). Only from `from` spark (2026-10-20: a romantic
# moment has to start it), and until that question has come, the spark it carries is applied but not shown.
spark_follow: per 25 cap 2 partner 3 cooldown 30 from 12
curve: 12 13 14 16 18 19 19 21 23 24 26 26 27 28 29 31 33 33 34 35 36 37 39 40 40 41 42 43 46 46 47 48 49 50 52 53 53 54 54 55 57 57 58 58 59 60 61 62

# ---------------- Presets (design §8.4): named groups of effects ----------------

@preset grind
params: skill
desc: Hard work on one skill.
do:
  $skill +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset rest
desc: A real rest.
do:
  mood +medium
  health +small

@preset sleep
desc: A night's sleep (bedtime, 2026-10-17): 8 Health and 4 Mood; at home on a break, 20 and 10. Taken when you go to bed, whatever your condition.
do:
  if break and has(plan_home):
    health += 20
    mood += 10
  else:
    health += 8
    mood += 4

@preset social
params: who
desc: Time with someone.
do:
  rel $who +small
  mood +small
  gold -tiny

@preset work
desc: Paid work.
do:
  gold +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset price_dear
desc: A dear price (world expansion 1, K3): what a shop asks for a special piece, 90 crowns.
do:
  gold -huge
  gold -large

@preset cure_dire
desc: The infirmary's full cure once you've needed it twice already (feedback 2026-10-25): 120 crowns.
do:
  gold -huge
  gold -huge

@preset price_fortune
desc: A small fortune, 150 crowns: what the rarest pieces cost.
do:
  gold -huge
  gold -huge
  gold -large

@preset splurge
desc: Spending to feel better.
do:
  mood +large
  gold -medium

@preset risk
params: res
desc: A gamble: a large gain or a medium loss.
do:
  chance even:
    $res +large
  else:
    $res -medium

# ---------------- Origins (docs/origin-design.md, 2026-10-16) ----------------
# Starting packages, applied before the first term's charges. Skills are XP grants through the ordinary XP cost
# (xp_cost: 1 0.04), calibrated to land on the design's levels from the base values in rules.grim: each grant is
# the sum of 1 + 0.04 × level from the base to the target (test/origins.test.js recomputes them). Purses are added
# to the base 30 crowns.

@preset origin_noble_start
desc: Charm 25, Lore 12; 60 crowns (90 with the 30 everyone starts with).
do:
  charm += 27.88
  lore += 5.52
  gold +huge

@preset origin_scholar_start
desc: Lore 28, Arcana 12; 30 crowns (60 with the 30 everyone starts with).
do:
  lore += 34
  arcana += 5.52
  gold +large

@preset origin_hedge_start
desc: Alchemy 30, Arcana 15, Lore 6; 15 crowns (45 with the 30 everyone starts with).
do:
  alchemy += 40.8
  arcana += 10.08
  lore -= 2
  gold +medium

@preset origin_street_start
desc: Guile 30, Vigor 18; 8 crowns (38 with the 30 everyone starts with).
do:
  guile += 40.8
  vigor += 15
  gold +small

@preset origin_merchant_start
desc: Charm 25, Guile 15; 120 crowns (150 with the 30 everyone starts with).
do:
  charm += 27.88
  guile += 12.6
  gold +huge
  gold +huge

# Support before each later term (terms 2–8), paid by the origin's funding card in the last break month. Cut by
# about a third from the design's amounts (2026-10-16: supported origins ended runs with several hundred crowns).
@preset noble_allowance
desc: The family's allowance, 38 crowns, and the expectations that come with it.
do:
  gold +large
  gold +small
  mood -small

@preset noble_gift
desc: A family gift on top, 11 crowns (30% of terms, rolled when the letter comes).
do:
  gold +small
  gold +tiny

@preset scholarship_stipend
desc: By the latest completed term's GPA: 3.5 or higher, 46 crowns (with an 8-crown merit bonus); 3.0 or higher, 38; below, nothing.
do:
  if term_gpa >= 3.5:
    gold +large
    gold +small
    gold +small
  elif term_gpa >= 3.0:
    gold +large
    gold +small

@preset trade_returns
desc: The company's share after a good trading period, 78 crowns (70% of terms, rolled when the report comes).
do:
  gold +huge
  gold +medium
  gold +tiny
